{"chunk_id": "5bc451683b36", "text": "King Dasaratha spends a night shattered by the consequences of the promise he gave Kaikeyi. Begging the night itself not to end, he pleads with her to abandon her demands and allow Rama\u2019s coronation. Kaikeyi remains unmoved and argues that truth and the keeping of vows are the highest form of dharma, citing ancient examples of kings who sacrificed even their bodies to uphold a promise. Bound by his word, Dasaratha collapses in despair, comparing himself to Bali trapped before Vamana. As dawn comes, the city of Ayodhya joyfully prepares for Rama\u2019s coronation\u2014streets decorated, priests assembled, sacred items gathered\u2014unaware of the catastrophe about to unfold. The sage Vasishtha arrives with the ritual materials, and the charioteer Sumantra enters to awaken the king, praising him and announcing that everything is ready, while the grief\u2011stricken monarch struggles under the weight of his vow.\nDasaratha laments helplessly as Kaikeyi insists on her boons\u2014Rama\u2019s exile and Bharata\u2019s coronation\u2014while Ayodhya unknowingly prepares for Rama\u2019s coronation.\nThemes: dharma vs attachment, power of vows, manipulation through righteousness, impending exile, tragic irony", "vector": [0.023372389376163483, -0.015806760638952255, -0.010423004627227783, -0.006417274475097656, -0.01637418195605278, 0.01577974110841751, -0.023129208013415337, -0.004019240383058786, -0.020089447498321533, -0.008214111439883709, 0.018292609602212906, 0.019116723909974098, 0.005366867873817682, 0.030910998582839966, -0.008126296103000641, 0.004363746847957373, 0.05182455852627754, -0.010240619070827961, 0.0312082190066576, -0.008416762575507164, -0.0005142263253219426, -0.008734248578548431, 0.0001980067027034238, 0.02335887961089611, -0.009740747511386871, 0.0019082948565483093, 0.01569868065416813, -0.024182992056012154, 0.024412663653492928, -0.0036038062535226345, -0.0011188011849299073, -0.009571871720254421, -0.002